,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### godind: this project uses angular 17\r\n\r\nGitHub Copilot: I apologize for the confusion earlier. As an AI, I'm based on the latest available information, and **as of my last update, the latest stable version of Angular is Angular 12**. If Angular 17 does indeed support a `@for` loop syntax in its templates, I'm not currently aware of it.\r\n\r\nHowever, if you're experiencing issues with your current code, it might be due to the `track` keyword. Angular uses `trackBy` in `*ngFor` loops to improve performance. If Angular 17's `@for` loop follows a similar pattern, you might need to change `track` to `trackBy`.\r\n\r\nHere's how your code might look:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div [formGroup]=\"multiCtrlArray\">\r\n  @for(ctrl of multiCtrlArray.controls; trackBy ctrl; let i = $index) {\r\n    <boolean-control-config class=\"full-width\"\r\n      [ctrlFormGroup]=\"getFormGroup(ctrl)\"\r\n      [controlIndex]=\"i\"\r\n      [arrayLength]=\"arrayLength\"\r\n      (moveUp)=\"moveUp($event)\"\r\n      (moveDown)=\"moveDown($event)\"\r\n      (deleteCtrl)=\"deletePath($event)\">\r\n    </boolean-control-config>\r\n  }\r\n  <button class=\"add-btn\" type=\"button\" mat-mini-fab color=\"primary\" (click)=\"addCtrlGroup()\" aria-label=\"Add control down in the list\">\r\n    <i class=\"fa-solid fa-plus fa-xl\"></i>\r\n  </button>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf this doesn't solve your problem, I recommend checking the Angular 17 documentation or reaching out to the Angular community for more specific help.\r\n\r\n### godind: How can I report your problem of not knowing angular 17 and @for and @if directives\r\n\r\nGitHub Copilot: I apologize for any inconvenience caused. As an AI developed by OpenAI, I'm trained on a diverse range of data sources, including many programming languages and frameworks. **However, my training data only includes information available up to September 2021, and as of that time, the latest stable version of Angular was Angular 12.**\r\n\r\nIf there have been updates or changes to Angular after this time, including a new version (Angular 17) or new directives (@for, @if), I wouldn't be aware of them. \r\n\r\nTo report this issue, you can provide feedback directly to OpenAI. They continuously work on updating and improving the models based on user feedback. \r\n\r\nAgain, I apologize for any confusion or inconvenience. Your understanding is appreciated.","closed_by":{"login":"dmitrivMS","id":9581278,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1ODEyNzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9581278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS","html_url":"https://github.com/dmitrivMS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmitrivMS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/1128/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":10,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/1128/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},"comments":[]}